  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I have an object I can parent back and forth between my hands, the world, and my head. It is set up fine in unity, but when I put it on my head it blocks my vision and appears halfway down through my head, while everybody else including the camera sees it fine.\n\nIf the object parented to the head has physbones, you would have to grab the local physbones. So people would expect to grab where they would see the object, but the physbones are physically lower down, ie: inside my face, but no one can see them. Only I can.\n\nI've found that this is the case for all head parents, so it's not an issue with anything I'm doing.",
